// =============================================================================
// SaaS platform Prisma fragment: TenantExportDownload
// =============================================================================
//
// REFERENCE SNIPPET — see 01-subscription.prisma for conventions.
//
// One row per download of a tenant's full export taken after its subscription
// ended: when, by which of the tenant's administrators, and how many bytes. The
// export itself is the application's, handed over through
// `TenantDataExportPort`; the row is written once the application has handed it
// over and before the file is sent, and it is the tenant's acknowledgement that
// the export was offered (`SC-PRIV-017`). It shows that the export was produced
// for that person at that moment, not that the browser saved it.
//
// As many rows per subscription as downloads were taken: there is no unique
// key, and a second download is a row of its own. They are read by the
// subscriptions whose end the tenant's views show, hence the index.
//
// Required wherever tenants are served, together with fragments 29 and 30.

model TenantExportDownload {
    id                 String   @id @default(uuid())
    // The tenant whose export was taken. Not a relation: the tenant model is the
    // application's.
    tenantId           String
    // The subscription whose end the export was offered for. Not a relation:
    // the record outlives the subscription row.
    subscriptionId     String
    // When the export was handed out, and to whom: an actor tag, as the audit
    // log writes it, and the user's id, as the session named them.
    downloadedAt       DateTime
    downloadedBy       String
    downloadedByUserId String
    // In bytes; an export can exceed what a 32-bit column holds.
    size               BigInt
    createdAt          DateTime @default(now())

    @@index([subscriptionId])
    @@map("tenant_export_downloads")
}
